  "evidence": [
    "Pinned 0x4C5240 computes this+group*24+0x2C and calls 0x4C5BF0: groups_[group]+8 is the list receiver. Group destructor4C5B80 and constructor4C5490 establish the contiguous head/tail/cursor/count fields.",
    "Keep WaveGroupList trivial with no user constructor/destructor; WaveControlGroup retains initialization/drain ordering, null-wave break and cursor preservation; groups_[16] remains 24-byte records.",
    "Five currently claimed list consumers4C5240,4C5280,4C5320,4C53A0,4C5400 and insert4C5BF0 retain identity and claims. Baseline/candidate measure wave_device,wave,sounddevice plus fresh build physical collateral and native layout verification.",
    "Baseline host tests: six pass, group_members fails because its harness lacks current wave_playback_device; legacy lifetime mutation test targets removed redirect wrappers. Migrate to actual product declarations/methods without weakening checks or changing production outside scope."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover the real typed list subobject at WaveControlGroup+8, remove five reinterpret views, preserve original group lifecycle and matching obligations; restore actual-source host controls.",
